{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CyAh363guhK6mH27jS5fpZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"exp-014 Naturalistic CC Validation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对 Common Crawl 2025-09/2026-01 snapshot 各抽 50K 文档，用训练好的 OBD-LightGBM  预测 depth distribution，与 AlignScore、vocabulary richness (type-token ratio,  hapax legomena ratio)、重复率 (self-BLEU) 做 Spearman correlation。 额外分析：按预测 depth 分层后各质量指标的分布变化。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"n_docs_per_snapshot\": 50000,\n7\t      \"predicted_depth_distribution\": {\n8\t        \"depth_0_pct\": 62.3,\n9\t        \"depth_1_pct\": 24.7,\n10\t        \"depth_2_pct\": 8.4,\n11\t        \"depth_3plus_pct\": 4.6\n12\t      },\n13\t      \"spearman_rho_alignscore_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.28,\n14\t      \"spearman_rho_alignscore_p\": \"<0.001\",\n15\t      \"spearman_rho_ttr_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.22,\n16\t      \"spearman_rho_ttr_p\": \"<0.001\",\n17\t      \"spearman_rho_hapax_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.19,\n18\t      \"spearman_rho_hapax_p\": \"<0.001\",\n19\t      \"spearman_rho_selfbleu_vs_predicted_depth\": 0.16,\n20\t      \"spearman_rho_selfbleu_p\": \"<0.001\",\n21\t      \"depth_stratified_alignscore_mean\": {\n22\t        \"depth_0\": 0.72,\n23\t        \"depth_1\": 0.65,\n24\t        \"depth_2\": 0.58,\n25\t        \"depth_3plus\": 0.51\n26\t      },\n27\t      \"depth_stratified_ttr_mean\": {\n28\t        \"depth_0\": 0.483,\n29\t        \"depth_1\": 0.451,\n30\t        \"depth_2\": 0.422,\n31\t        \"depth_3plus\": 0.398\n32\t      },\n33\t      \"snapshot_temporal_shift\": {\n34\t        \"cc_2025_09_mean_depth\": 0.58,\n35\t        \"cc_2026_01_mean_depth\": 0.64,\n36\t        \"delta\": 0.06,\n37\t        \"p_ks_test\": 0.032\n38\t      },\n39\t      \"cross_validation_with_lab_features\": {\n40\t        \"feature_rank_spearman_lab_vs_wild\": 0.81,\n41\t        \"top3_wild_features\": [\n42\t          \"freq_entropy\",\n43\t          \"surp_d1_mean\",\n44\t          \"surp_std\"\n45\t        ]\n46\t      }\n47\t    },\n48\t    \"tables\": [\n49\t      {\n50\t        \"name\": \"Table: CC Depth Distribution vs Quality Metrics\",\n51\t        \"columns\": [\n52\t          \"Predicted Depth\",\n53\t          \"N docs\",\n54\t          \"AlignScore (mean±std)\",\n55\t          \"TTR (mean±std)\",\n56\t          \"Self-BLEU (mean±std)\"\n57\t        ],\n58\t        \"rows\": [\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"0 (human)\",\n61\t            \"~31K\",\n62\t            \"0.72±0.11\",\n63\t            \"0.483±0.052\",\n64\t            \"0.12±0.04\"\n65\t          ],\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"1\",\n68\t            \"~12K\",\n69\t            \"0.65±0.13\",\n70\t            \"0.451±0.058\",\n71\t            \"0.15±0.05\"\n72\t          ],\n73\t          [\n74\t            \"2\",\n75\t            \"~4K\",\n76\t            \"0.58±0.14\",\n77\t            \"0.422±0.061\",\n78\t            \"0.19±0.06\"\n79\t          ],\n80\t          [\n81\t            \"3+\",\n82\t            \"~2K\",\n83\t            \"0.51±0.16\",\n84\t            \"0.398±0.067\",\n85\t            \"0.23±0.07\"\n86\t          ]\n87\t        ]\n88\t      },\n89\t      {\n90\t        \"name\": \"Table: Spearman Correlations (Predicted Depth vs Quality)\",\n91\t        \"columns\": [\n92\t          \"Quality Metric\",\n93\t          \"ρ\",\n94\t          \"p-value\",\n95\t          \"95% CI\"\n96\t        ],\n97\t        \"rows\": [\n98\t          [\n99\t            \"AlignScore\",\n100\t            \"-0.28\",\n101\t            \"<0.001\",\n102\t            \"[-0.30, -0.26]\"\n103\t          ],\n104\t          [\n105\t            \"Type-Token Ratio\",\n106\t            \"-0.22\",\n107\t            \"<0.001\",\n108\t            \"[-0.24, -0.20]\"\n109\t          ],\n110\t          [\n111\t            \"Hapax Ratio\",\n112\t            \"-0.19\",\n113\t            \"<0.001\",\n114\t            \"[-0.21, -0.17]\"\n115\t          ],\n116\t          [\n117\t            \"Self-BLEU\",\n118\t            \"+0.16\",\n119\t            \"<0.001\",\n120\t            \"[+0.14, +0.18]\"\n121\t          ]\n122\t        ]\n123\t      }\n124\t    ],\n125\t    \"figures\": [],\n126\t    \"analysis\": \"Naturalistic validation 提供了方向性证据但不是 decisive。核心限制：我们的 depth  predictor 训练于 prompt-chain controlled data，而 wild 合成文本的生成路径多样化且未知。 ρ~0.25 的 moderate correlation 足以进入 Discussion 作为 \\\"promising direction\\\"， 但审稿人不会将其视为强 external validity 证据。Median 档审稿人的典型反应： \\\"The naturalistic analysis is interesting but the modest correlations (ρ<0.30)  raise questions about whether the lab-measured K* translates to actionable  web-scale data governance\\\" — 这成为 major weakness #2 但不致命。 建议在论文中定位为 \\\"preliminary naturalistic analysis\\\" 而非 \\\"validation\\\"， 并在 Limitations 中讨论 lab-to-wild gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，lab-to-wild 迁移部分成功但受限。Spearman ρ~0.22-0.28 统计显著但 practically  moderate，原因有三：(1) CC 真实数据包含多种非 prompt-chain 的合成路径（翻译管道、摘要重写、 RAG 输出），这些与训练时的 prompt-chain 分布不同；(2) CC 包含大量非英文和低质量原始文本， 引入与 depth 无关的噪声；(3) 深度预测在 depth≥2 处 uncertainty 急剧增大（lab 中 2v3 AUC  仅 0.55-0.56），导致高 depth 预测噪声大。正向信号来自 depth-stratified quality 单调递减—— 预测的更深层文本确实质量更低——但效应大小不足以支持 \\\"operational deployment\\\" claim。 时间维度的 CC 2025→2026 depth 增长（+0.06）与合成文本扩散趋势一致但统计上 borderline。 审稿人会认为这是 \\\"suggestive but not definitive\\\" 的 preliminary validation， 一位审稿人可能要求排除明显的机器翻译文本后重做分析。Feature ranking 在 lab 和 wild 之间  ρ=0.81 说明特征空间迁移合理，但不完美——wild 数据中 freq_entropy 的重要性上升， 因为不同合成路径产生不同的词汇分布。\\n\"\n127\t  },\n128\t  {\n129\t    \"name\": \"exp-028 Subsampling Power Curve\",\n130\t    \"description\": \"对 C4 数据（使用 exp-007 的 Qwen-cont 和 Pythia 数据），在 n={1000, 2000, 3000, 4000, 5000}  各做 10 次 bootstrap resample，每次重新计算 1v2 pairwise AUC 和 K* 判定， 绘制 power curve：在各 n 下 K*=2 判定的成功率（即 1v2 CI lower > θ=0.60 的比例）。\\n\",\n131\t    \"results\": {\n132\t      \"models_tested\": [\n133\t        \"Qwen-cont (most marginal)\",\n134\t        \"Pythia-1.4B (moderate margin)\"\n135\t      ],\n136\t      \"resamples_per_n\": 10,\n137\t      \"qwen_cont_power_curve\": {\n138\t        \"n_1000\": {\n139\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.3,\n140\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.61,\n141\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.038,\n142\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.591\n143\t        },\n144\t        \"n_2000\": {\n145\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.5,\n146\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n147\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.027,\n148\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.597\n149\t        },\n150\t        \"n_3000\": {\n151\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.7,\n152\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n153\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.022,\n154\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.6\n155\t        },\n156\t        \"n_4000\": {\n157\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.9,\n158\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n159\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.019,\n160\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.602\n161\t        },\n162\t        \"n_5000\": {\n163\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n164\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n165\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.017,\n166\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.603\n167\t        }\n168\t      },\n169\t      \"pythia_power_curve\": {\n170\t        \"n_1000\": {\n171\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.7,\n172\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.653,\n173\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.035,\n174\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.636\n175\t        },\n176\t        \"n_2000\": {\n177\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.9,\n178\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n179\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.025,\n180\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.641\n181\t        },\n182\t        \"n_3000\": {\n183\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n184\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n185\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.02,\n186\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.644\n187\t        },\n188\t        \"n_4000\": {\n189\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n190\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n191\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.018,\n192\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.645\n193\t        },\n194\t        \"n_5000\": {\n195\t          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n196\t          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n197\t          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.016,\n198\t          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.646\n199\t        }\n200\t      },\n201\t      \"critical_n_for_95pct_power\": {\n202\t        \"qwen_cont\": 4500,\n203\t        \"pythia\": 2000\n204\t      },\n205\t      \"arXiv_implication\": {\n206\t        \"arXiv_n_per_model\": 2200,\n207\t        \"arXiv_2v3_effect_size\": \"larger (AUC~0.63-0.65)\",\n208\t        \"arXiv_power_sufficient\": true,\n209\t        \"note\": \"arXiv 的 2v3 AUC 效应量 (0.63-0.65) 远大于 C4 1v2 (0.61)，n=2200 足够\"\n210\t      }\n211\t    },\n212\t    \"tables\": [\n213\t      {\n214\t        \"name\": \"Table: K*=2 Detection Power by Sample Size\",\n215\t        \"columns\": [\n216\t          \"n\",\n217\t          \"Qwen-cont Success Rate\",\n218\t          \"Qwen-cont mean CI lower\",\n219\t          \"Pythia Success Rate\",\n220\t          \"Pythia mean CI lower\"\n221\t        ],\n222\t        \"rows\": [\n223\t          [\n224\t            \"1,000\",\n225\t            \"3/10\",\n226\t            \"0.591\",\n227\t            \"7/10\",\n228\t            \"0.636\"\n229\t          ],\n230\t          [\n231\t            \"2,000\",\n232\t            \"5/10\",\n233\t            \"0.597\",\n234\t            \"9/10\",\n235\t            \"0.641\"\n236\t          ],\n237\t          [\n238\t            \"3,000\",\n239\t            \"7/10\",\n240\t            \"0.600\",\n241\t            \"10/10\",\n242\t            \"0.644\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"4,000\",\n246\t            \"9/10\",\n247\t            \"0.602\",\n248\t            \"10/10\",\n249\t            \"0.645\"\n250\t          ],\n251\t          [\n252\t            \"5,000\",\n253\t            \"10/10\",\n254\t            \"0.603\",\n255\t            \"10/10\",\n256\t            \"0.646\"\n257\t          ]\n258\t        ]\n259\t      }\n260\t    ],\n261\t    \"figures\": [],\n262\t    \"analysis\": \"Power curve 的核心价值在于 rebuttal。当审稿人质疑 Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015  的 marginal 性时，power curve 提供了量化回应：\\\"At n=5000, even the most marginal  configuration (Qwen-cont, AUC=0.611) achieves 100% K*=2 detection rate.  The marginality reflects a genuine small effect size for this particular  model in continuation mode, not insufficient evidence.\\\" 同时 power curve 暴露了一个 honest limitation：如果有模型的 1v2 AUC 在 0.600-0.605  范围内（比 Qwen-cont 更边缘），n=5000 可能不够。这在 median 档下被审稿人标记为  minor concern 但可以通过 \\\"our protocol can be scaled to larger n for  borderline cases\\\" 来回应。 Rebuttal 用途：直接回应 θ=0.60 任意性质疑——power analysis 表明在合理的 n 下， θ±0.02 范围内的 K* 判定结果一致（AUC 0.58 的 pair 在任何 n 下都不通过， AUC 0.63+ 的 pair 在 n≥1500 下就通过），证明 θ=0.60 处存在 natural gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 power curve 揭示了已知的 Qwen-cont 边缘性问题的样本量根源。 Qwen-cont 1v2 AUC=0.6112 仅超过 θ=0.60 约 0.011，这意味着 CI lower > θ  需要很窄的 CI，即大样本。在 n=1000 时 CI width~0.038，CI lower~0.591 < 0.60， 导致 K*=2 判定失败率 70%。n=3000 是转折点（成功率 70%），n≥4500 才达到 95% power。 相比之下 Pythia 1v2 AUC=0.6539，margin 大得多，n=2000 即可达 90% power。 这为审稿人提供了两个信息：(1) 现有 n=5000 的主实验样本量充分（Qwen-cont 100% 通过）， (2) Qwen-cont 的边缘性是效应量问题而非方法论缺陷。 arXiv 实验 n=2200 但效应量更大（2v3 AUC 0.63-0.65），power 充足。 审稿人可能的反应：承认现有样本量 adequate，但指出 \\\"the marginal Qwen-cont result  suggests that for some model configurations, considerably larger samples would  be needed to confidently determine K*\\\"，这成为 minor weakness。\\n\"\n263\t  },\n264\t  {\n265\t    \"name\": \"exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated (what-if)\",\n266\t    \"description\": \"将 exp-026 arXiv graduated filtering 负向结果整合进论文：Section 5 增加 arXiv null  result 表格，Discussion 增加 \\\"K* characterizes discriminability not data utility\\\" 洞察， Appendix 放完整 15-run paired t-test 表。评估对审稿分数和 credibility 的影响。\\n\",\n267\t    \"results\": {\n268\t      \"section_5_addition\": {\n269\t        \"table_rows\": 3,\n270\t        \"table_content\": \"no_filter/binary/graduated on arXiv, MMLU and HellaSwag means±std\",\n271\t        \"paired_ttest_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_p\": 0.94,\n272\t        \"paired_ttest_graduated_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_p\": 0.89,\n273\t        \"paired_ttest_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_p\": 0.005,\n274\t        \"paired_ttest_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_p\": \"<0.001\",\n275\t        \"binary_direction_conflict\": \"MMLU -0.23pp vs HellaSwag +0.42pp\"\n276\t      },\n277\t      \"discussion_insight\": {\n278\t        \"key_sentence\": \"K* characterizes the statistical discriminability boundary of recursive  generation, not a utility boundary — text at depth 2-3 is distinguishable  from depth 3-4 on arXiv (2v3 AUC=0.64), but this discriminability does not  translate to meaningful quality differences for downstream training.\\n\"\n279\t      },\n280\t      \"reviewer_reactions\": {\n281\t        \"reviewer_1_positive\": \"\\\"The honest reporting of the arXiv null result (exp-026) is appreciated  and strengthens the paper's credibility. The reframing of K* as a  discriminability measure rather than a utility measure is insightful.\\\"\\n\",\n282\t        \"reviewer_2_negative\": \"\\\"The arXiv filtering result essentially means that K*-aware curation only  works on C4 with one model family (Qwen). Combined with exp-025 (Pythia  null), the practical value of C3 is limited to a narrow setting.\\\"\\n\",\n283\t        \"reviewer_3_neutral\": \"\\\"Honest negative results are expected in scientific practice, not bonus  points. The C3 claim should be explicitly conditional on model and domain.\\\"\\n\"\n284\t      },\n285\t      \"credibility_delta\": \"+0.15 to +0.25 on overall score (partial offset by C3 weakening)\",\n286\t      \"c3_acceptance_prob_impact\": \"-0.10 (from 0.55 to 0.45)\",\n287\t      \"honest_negative_recognition\": \"acknowledged by 2/3 reviewers but not viewed as special merit\",\n288\t      \"net_paper_impact\": {\n289\t        \"arr_score_without_integration\": 3.15,\n290\t        \"arr_score_with_integration\": 3.25,\n291\t        \"findings_prob_without\": 0.7,\n292\t        \"findings_prob_with\": 0.78\n293\t      }\n294\t    },\n295\t    \"tables\": [\n296\t      {\n297\t        \"name\": \"Table: arXiv Filtering Results (Section 5 addition)\",\n298\t        \"columns\": [\n299\t          \"Strategy\",\n300\t          \"MMLU\",\n301\t          \"HellaSwag\",\n302\t          \"Δ MMLU vs no-filter\",\n303\t          \"Δ HellaSwag vs no-filter\"\n304\t        ],\n305\t        \"rows\": [\n306\t          [\n307\t            \"No filter\",\n308\t            \"0.5899±0.0008\",\n309\t            \"0.6600±0.0002\",\n310\t            \"—\",\n311\t            \"—\"\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"Binary\",\n315\t            \"0.5876±0.0004\",\n316\t            \"0.6642±0.0004\",\n317\t            \"-0.0023 (p=0.005)\",\n318\t            \"+0.0042 (p<0.001)\"\n319\t          ],\n320\t          [\n321\t            \"Graduated α=0.9\",\n322\t            \"0.5900±0.0011\",\n323\t            \"0.6599±0.0003\",\n324\t            \"+0.0001 (p=0.94)\",\n325\t            \"-0.0001 (p=0.89)\"\n326\t          ]\n327\t        ]\n328\t      }\n329\t    ],\n330\t    \"figures\": [],\n331\t    \"analysis\": \"整合策略：在 Section 5 增加一段 \\\"Domain Generalization of Filtering\\\" 小节， 先呈 C4 正向结果（binary > graduated ≈ no-filter），再呈 arXiv null result  （graduated ≈ no-filter, binary 有 metric-specific trade-off），最后 Pythia  null result（所有策略 indistinguishable）。Discussion 中将 C3 重新定位： \\\"These results reveal that K* characterizes the boundary of statistical  discriminability in recursive generations, not a boundary of training data  utility. The arXiv domain sustains discrimination to K*=3, meaning depth-2  and depth-3 texts are statistically distinguishable — but this distinguishability  does not translate to differential value for language model training.\\\" 这个 reframing 实际上增加了 K* 概念的信息论深度——K* 是 information-theoretic  measurement，不是 utility metric。在 median 档下，一位审稿人会认为这是  \\\"more honest and nuanced\\\" framing，另一位会用它来论证 practical impact 不足。\\n\\nMedian 档下，诚实报告负向结果是双刃剑。正面：(1) 增加科学可信度——审稿人看到作者不 cherry-pick 结果；(2) \\\"K* ≠ data utility\\\" 洞察为 K* 概念提供了更深层理解，从  \\\"K* predicts optimal curation\\\" 转为更 nuanced 的 \\\"K* measures statistical  discriminability whose practical implications are domain- and model-dependent\\\"。 负面：(1) C3 的 practical claim 从 \\\"K*-aware filtering outperforms\\\" 被迫降级为  \\\"binary filtering suffices for web text; graduated filtering provides no  additional benefit\\\"——这削弱了论文的 practical impact story；(2) 两个负向 filtering  结果（exp-025 Pythia, exp-026 arXiv）加上 exp-006 仅 Qwen-C4 正向结果，让审稿人 总结为 \\\"filtering benefit is model-specific and domain-specific\\\"；(3) 审稿人认为 honest negative 是 expected practice 而非加分项——\\\"we don't give extra credit  for not lying\\\"。 净效应在 median 档下是 slightly positive：credibility gain (+0.1-0.15 on score)  略大于 practical claim 损失，因为 C1' 是论文核心且不受影响。Findings 概率从 0.70  提升到 0.78，因为 Findings track 更看重 characterization quality 而非 practical impact。\\n\"\n332\t  }\n333\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b77da2b-c5ce-4f78-bfc2-dad27a2f0048","uuid":"5633b6b2-432a-403c-b1c2-31e45afe2916","timestamp":"2026-05-18T12:48:10.130Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_7/projects/gen-depth-contamination/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T123349/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-014 Naturalistic CC Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"对 Common Crawl 2025-09/2026-01 snapshot 各抽 50K 文档，用训练好的 OBD-LightGBM  预测 depth distribution，与 AlignScore、vocabulary richness (type-token ratio,  hapax legomena ratio)、重复率 (self-BLEU) 做 Spearman correlation。 额外分析：按预测 depth 分层后各质量指标的分布变化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_docs_per_snapshot\": 50000,\n      \"predicted_depth_distribution\": {\n        \"depth_0_pct\": 62.3,\n        \"depth_1_pct\": 24.7,\n        \"depth_2_pct\": 8.4,\n        \"depth_3plus_pct\": 4.6\n      },\n      \"spearman_rho_alignscore_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.28,\n      \"spearman_rho_alignscore_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"spearman_rho_ttr_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.22,\n      \"spearman_rho_ttr_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"spearman_rho_hapax_vs_predicted_depth\": -0.19,\n      \"spearman_rho_hapax_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"spearman_rho_selfbleu_vs_predicted_depth\": 0.16,\n      \"spearman_rho_selfbleu_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"depth_stratified_alignscore_mean\": {\n        \"depth_0\": 0.72,\n        \"depth_1\": 0.65,\n        \"depth_2\": 0.58,\n        \"depth_3plus\": 0.51\n      },\n      \"depth_stratified_ttr_mean\": {\n        \"depth_0\": 0.483,\n        \"depth_1\": 0.451,\n        \"depth_2\": 0.422,\n        \"depth_3plus\": 0.398\n      },\n      \"snapshot_temporal_shift\": {\n        \"cc_2025_09_mean_depth\": 0.58,\n        \"cc_2026_01_mean_depth\": 0.64,\n        \"delta\": 0.06,\n        \"p_ks_test\": 0.032\n      },\n      \"cross_validation_with_lab_features\": {\n        \"feature_rank_spearman_lab_vs_wild\": 0.81,\n        \"top3_wild_features\": [\n          \"freq_entropy\",\n          \"surp_d1_mean\",\n          \"surp_std\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: CC Depth Distribution vs Quality Metrics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predicted Depth\",\n          \"N docs\",\n          \"AlignScore (mean±std)\",\n          \"TTR (mean±std)\",\n          \"Self-BLEU (mean±std)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (human)\",\n            \"~31K\",\n            \"0.72±0.11\",\n            \"0.483±0.052\",\n            \"0.12±0.04\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1\",\n            \"~12K\",\n            \"0.65±0.13\",\n            \"0.451±0.058\",\n            \"0.15±0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2\",\n            \"~4K\",\n            \"0.58±0.14\",\n            \"0.422±0.061\",\n            \"0.19±0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3+\",\n            \"~2K\",\n            \"0.51±0.16\",\n            \"0.398±0.067\",\n            \"0.23±0.07\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Spearman Correlations (Predicted Depth vs Quality)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Quality Metric\",\n          \"ρ\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"AlignScore\",\n            \"-0.28\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"[-0.30, -0.26]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Type-Token Ratio\",\n            \"-0.22\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"[-0.24, -0.20]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hapax Ratio\",\n            \"-0.19\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"[-0.21, -0.17]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Self-BLEU\",\n            \"+0.16\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"[+0.14, +0.18]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Naturalistic validation 提供了方向性证据但不是 decisive。核心限制：我们的 depth  predictor 训练于 prompt-chain controlled data，而 wild 合成文本的生成路径多样化且未知。 ρ~0.25 的 moderate correlation 足以进入 Discussion 作为 \\\"promising direction\\\"， 但审稿人不会将其视为强 external validity 证据。Median 档审稿人的典型反应： \\\"The naturalistic analysis is interesting but the modest correlations (ρ<0.30)  raise questions about whether the lab-measured K* translates to actionable  web-scale data governance\\\" — 这成为 major weakness #2 但不致命。 建议在论文中定位为 \\\"preliminary naturalistic analysis\\\" 而非 \\\"validation\\\"， 并在 Limitations 中讨论 lab-to-wild gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，lab-to-wild 迁移部分成功但受限。Spearman ρ~0.22-0.28 统计显著但 practically  moderate，原因有三：(1) CC 真实数据包含多种非 prompt-chain 的合成路径（翻译管道、摘要重写、 RAG 输出），这些与训练时的 prompt-chain 分布不同；(2) CC 包含大量非英文和低质量原始文本， 引入与 depth 无关的噪声；(3) 深度预测在 depth≥2 处 uncertainty 急剧增大（lab 中 2v3 AUC  仅 0.55-0.56），导致高 depth 预测噪声大。正向信号来自 depth-stratified quality 单调递减—— 预测的更深层文本确实质量更低——但效应大小不足以支持 \\\"operational deployment\\\" claim。 时间维度的 CC 2025→2026 depth 增长（+0.06）与合成文本扩散趋势一致但统计上 borderline。 审稿人会认为这是 \\\"suggestive but not definitive\\\" 的 preliminary validation， 一位审稿人可能要求排除明显的机器翻译文本后重做分析。Feature ranking 在 lab 和 wild 之间  ρ=0.81 说明特征空间迁移合理，但不完美——wild 数据中 freq_entropy 的重要性上升， 因为不同合成路径产生不同的词汇分布。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp-028 Subsampling Power Curve\",\n    \"description\": \"对 C4 数据（使用 exp-007 的 Qwen-cont 和 Pythia 数据），在 n={1000, 2000, 3000, 4000, 5000}  各做 10 次 bootstrap resample，每次重新计算 1v2 pairwise AUC 和 K* 判定， 绘制 power curve：在各 n 下 K*=2 判定的成功率（即 1v2 CI lower > θ=0.60 的比例）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"models_tested\": [\n        \"Qwen-cont (most marginal)\",\n        \"Pythia-1.4B (moderate margin)\"\n      ],\n      \"resamples_per_n\": 10,\n      \"qwen_cont_power_curve\": {\n        \"n_1000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.3,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.61,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.038,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.591\n        },\n        \"n_2000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.5,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.027,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.597\n        },\n        \"n_3000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.7,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.022,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.6\n        },\n        \"n_4000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.9,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.019,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.602\n        },\n        \"n_5000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.611,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.017,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.603\n        }\n      },\n      \"pythia_power_curve\": {\n        \"n_1000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.7,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.653,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.035,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.636\n        },\n        \"n_2000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 0.9,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.025,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.641\n        },\n        \"n_3000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.02,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.644\n        },\n        \"n_4000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.018,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.645\n        },\n        \"n_5000\": {\n          \"kstar2_success_rate\": 1.0,\n          \"mean_1v2_auc\": 0.654,\n          \"mean_ci_width\": 0.016,\n          \"mean_ci_lower\": 0.646\n        }\n      },\n      \"critical_n_for_95pct_power\": {\n        \"qwen_cont\": 4500,\n        \"pythia\": 2000\n      },\n      \"arXiv_implication\": {\n        \"arXiv_n_per_model\": 2200,\n        \"arXiv_2v3_effect_size\": \"larger (AUC~0.63-0.65)\",\n        \"arXiv_power_sufficient\": true,\n        \"note\": \"arXiv 的 2v3 AUC 效应量 (0.63-0.65) 远大于 C4 1v2 (0.61)，n=2200 足够\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: K*=2 Detection Power by Sample Size\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n\",\n          \"Qwen-cont Success Rate\",\n          \"Qwen-cont mean CI lower\",\n          \"Pythia Success Rate\",\n          \"Pythia mean CI lower\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1,000\",\n            \"3/10\",\n            \"0.591\",\n            \"7/10\",\n            \"0.636\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2,000\",\n            \"5/10\",\n            \"0.597\",\n            \"9/10\",\n            \"0.641\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3,000\",\n            \"7/10\",\n            \"0.600\",\n            \"10/10\",\n            \"0.644\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4,000\",\n            \"9/10\",\n            \"0.602\",\n            \"10/10\",\n            \"0.645\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5,000\",\n            \"10/10\",\n            \"0.603\",\n            \"10/10\",\n            \"0.646\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Power curve 的核心价值在于 rebuttal。当审稿人质疑 Qwen-cont CI lower=0.6015  的 marginal 性时，power curve 提供了量化回应：\\\"At n=5000, even the most marginal  configuration (Qwen-cont, AUC=0.611) achieves 100% K*=2 detection rate.  The marginality reflects a genuine small effect size for this particular  model in continuation mode, not insufficient evidence.\\\" 同时 power curve 暴露了一个 honest limitation：如果有模型的 1v2 AUC 在 0.600-0.605  范围内（比 Qwen-cont 更边缘），n=5000 可能不够。这在 median 档下被审稿人标记为  minor concern 但可以通过 \\\"our protocol can be scaled to larger n for  borderline cases\\\" 来回应。 Rebuttal 用途：直接回应 θ=0.60 任意性质疑——power analysis 表明在合理的 n 下， θ±0.02 范围内的 K* 判定结果一致（AUC 0.58 的 pair 在任何 n 下都不通过， AUC 0.63+ 的 pair 在 n≥1500 下就通过），证明 θ=0.60 处存在 natural gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下 power curve 揭示了已知的 Qwen-cont 边缘性问题的样本量根源。 Qwen-cont 1v2 AUC=0.6112 仅超过 θ=0.60 约 0.011，这意味着 CI lower > θ  需要很窄的 CI，即大样本。在 n=1000 时 CI width~0.038，CI lower~0.591 < 0.60， 导致 K*=2 判定失败率 70%。n=3000 是转折点（成功率 70%），n≥4500 才达到 95% power。 相比之下 Pythia 1v2 AUC=0.6539，margin 大得多，n=2000 即可达 90% power。 这为审稿人提供了两个信息：(1) 现有 n=5000 的主实验样本量充分（Qwen-cont 100% 通过）， (2) Qwen-cont 的边缘性是效应量问题而非方法论缺陷。 arXiv 实验 n=2200 但效应量更大（2v3 AUC 0.63-0.65），power 充足。 审稿人可能的反应：承认现有样本量 adequate，但指出 \\\"the marginal Qwen-cont result  suggests that for some model configurations, considerably larger samples would  be needed to confidently determine K*\\\"，这成为 minor weakness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"exp_026_arxiv_filtering_integrated (what-if)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 exp-026 arXiv graduated filtering 负向结果整合进论文：Section 5 增加 arXiv null  result 表格，Discussion 增加 \\\"K* characterizes discriminability not data utility\\\" 洞察， Appendix 放完整 15-run paired t-test 表。评估对审稿分数和 credibility 的影响。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"section_5_addition\": {\n        \"table_rows\": 3,\n        \"table_content\": \"no_filter/binary/graduated on arXiv, MMLU and HellaSwag means±std\",\n        \"paired_ttest_graduated_vs_nofilter_mmlu_p\": 0.94,\n        \"paired_ttest_graduated_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_p\": 0.89,\n        \"paired_ttest_binary_vs_nofilter_mmlu_p\": 0.005,\n        \"paired_ttest_binary_vs_nofilter_hellaswag_p\": \"<0.001\",\n        \"binary_direction_conflict\": \"MMLU -0.23pp vs HellaSwag +0.42pp\"\n      },\n      \"discussion_insight\": {\n        \"key_sentence\": \"K* characterizes the statistical discriminability boundary of recursive  generation, not a utility boundary — text at depth 2-3 is distinguishable  from depth 3-4 on arXiv (2v3 AUC=0.64), but this discriminability does not  translate to meaningful quality differences for downstream training.\\n\"\n      },\n      \"reviewer_reactions\": {\n        \"reviewer_1_positive\": \"\\\"The honest reporting of the arXiv null result (exp-026) is appreciated  and strengthens the paper's credibility. The reframing of K* as a  discriminability measure rather than a utility measure is insightful.\\\"\\n\",\n        \"reviewer_2_negative\": \"\\\"The arXiv filtering result essentially means that K*-aware curation only  works on C4 with one model family (Qwen). Combined with exp-025 (Pythia  null), the practical value of C3 is limited to a narrow setting.\\\"\\n\",\n        \"reviewer_3_neutral\": \"\\\"Honest negative results are expected in scientific practice, not bonus  points. The C3 claim should be explicitly conditional on model and domain.\\\"\\n\"\n      },\n      \"credibility_delta\": \"+0.15 to +0.25 on overall score (partial offset by C3 weakening)\",\n      \"c3_acceptance_prob_impact\": \"-0.10 (from 0.55 to 0.45)\",\n      \"honest_negative_recognition\": \"acknowledged by 2/3 reviewers but not viewed as special merit\",\n      \"net_paper_impact\": {\n        \"arr_score_without_integration\": 3.15,\n        \"arr_score_with_integration\": 3.25,\n        \"findings_prob_without\": 0.7,\n        \"findings_prob_with\": 0.78\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: arXiv Filtering Results (Section 5 addition)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Strategy\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"Δ MMLU vs no-filter\",\n          \"Δ HellaSwag vs no-filter\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"No filter\",\n            \"0.5899±0.0008\",\n            \"0.6600±0.0002\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Binary\",\n            \"0.5876±0.0004\",\n            \"0.6642±0.0004\",\n            \"-0.0023 (p=0.005)\",\n            \"+0.0042 (p<0.001)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Graduated α=0.9\",\n            \"0.5900±0.0011\",\n            \"0.6599±0.0003\",\n            \"+0.0001 (p=0.94)\",\n            \"-0.0001 (p=0.89)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"整合策略：在 Section 5 增加一段 \\\"Domain Generalization of Filtering\\\" 小节， 先呈 C4 正向结果（binary > graduated ≈ no-filter），再呈 arXiv null result  （graduated ≈ no-filter, binary 有 metric-specific trade-off），最后 Pythia  null result（所有策略 indistinguishable）。Discussion 中将 C3 重新定位： \\\"These results reveal that K* characterizes the boundary of statistical  discriminability in recursive generations, not a boundary of training data  utility. The arXiv domain sustains discrimination to K*=3, meaning depth-2  and depth-3 texts are statistically distinguishable — but this distinguishability  does not translate to differential value for language model training.\\\" 这个 reframing 实际上增加了 K* 概念的信息论深度——K* 是 information-theoretic  measurement，不是 utility metric。在 median 档下，一位审稿人会认为这是  \\\"more honest and nuanced\\\" framing，另一位会用它来论证 practical impact 不足。\\n\\nMedian 档下，诚实报告负向结果是双刃剑。正面：(1) 增加科学可信度——审稿人看到作者不 cherry-pick 结果；(2) \\\"K* ≠ data utility\\\" 洞察为 K* 概念提供了更深层理解，从  \\\"K* predicts optimal curation\\\" 转为更 nuanced 的 \\\"K* measures statistical  discriminability whose practical implications are domain- and model-dependent\\\"。 负面：(1) C3 的 practical claim 从 \\\"K*-aware filtering outperforms\\\" 被迫降级为  \\\"binary filtering suffices for web text; graduated filtering provides no  additional benefit\\\"——这削弱了论文的 practical impact story；(2) 两个负向 filtering  结果（exp-025 Pythia, exp-026 arXiv）加上 exp-006 仅 Qwen-C4 正向结果，让审稿人 总结为 \\\"filtering benefit is model-specific and domain-specific\\\"；(3) 审稿人认为 honest negative 是 expected practice 而非加分项——\\\"we don't give extra credit  for not lying\\\"。 净效应在 median 档下是 slightly positive：credibility gain (+0.1-0.15 on score)  略大于 practical claim 损失，因为 C1' 是论文核心且不受影响。Findings 概率从 0.70  提升到 0.78，因为 Findings track 更看重 characterization quality 而非 practical impact。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":333,"startLine":1,"totalLines":333}}}
